Training datasets
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The model was trained on the following datasets. No dataset images are
redistributed in this repository.

Nutrition5k (Google Research), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0).
https://github.com/google-research-datasets/Nutrition5k
  Thames, Q., Karpur, A., Norris, W., Xia, F., Panait, L., Weyand, T., Sim, J.
  "Nutrition5k: Towards Automatic Nutritional Understanding of Generic Food."
  Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern
  Recognition (CVPR), 2021, pp. 8903-8911.

SNAPMe, Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0).
https://doi.org/10.15482/USDA.ADC/1528346
  Chin, E. L., Larke, J. A., Bouzid, Y. Y., Nguyen, T., Vainberg, Y.,
  Smilowitz, J. T., Lemay, D. "SNAPMe: A Benchmark Dataset of Food Photos
  with Food Records for Evaluation of Computer Vision Algorithms in the
  Context of Dietary Assessment." Ag Data Commons, 2022.
  Larke, J. A., et al. "Surveying Nutrient Assessment with Photographs of
  Meals (SNAPMe): A Benchmark Dataset of Food Photos for Dietary Assessment."
  Nutrients 15(23):4972, 2023. https://www.mdpi.com/2072-6643/15/23/4972
